{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "feature": "mobile-rendering-recovery",
  "scope": "Stable legible lighting as the camera moves, clear high-density phone rendering with usable quality choices, recovery after mobile backgrounding or graphics loss that preserves the world and authoring session, and intuitive house interior entry and exterior return with playable desktop/phone controls.",
  "criticAgent": "Luna",
  "builderAgent": "/root",
  "decision": "changes_requested",
  "grades": {
    "intuitiveness": {
      "grade": "B+",
      "evidence": "The retained renderer and mobile journeys demonstrate reachable movement, authoring, quality, drawer, Export and retry controls across the declared desktop-emulated phone layouts. The corrected saved-workspace path now gives a useful retry message for immediate read abort, late abort and synchronous JavaScript failure, and the delayed-entry journey preserves the authoring mask and both histories through cancellation and recovery. Physical phone control and lifecycle behavior remain unverified."
    },
    "accuracy": {
      "grade": "B",
      "evidence": "Source inspection confirms that saved data remains private until IndexedDB transaction completion, with request-error, transaction-abort and synchronous-throw handling. Retained final evidence covers 35 storage assertions and 24 entry/recovery assertions, including exact world/history/future/selection/camera comparisons and a successful retry. The evidence is desktop Chromium instrumentation with deterministic faults; it does not cover the affected physical Android/Brave device, named-room-plan loss with fresh picking, or every blocked/quota database path."
    },
    "wowFactor": {
      "grade": "B",
      "evidence": "The retained captures show furnished interiors, exterior return and coherent high-density controls, while recovery retains a populated authoring session rather than resetting the world. The full scope still lacks same-surface camera-angle sweeps and final affected-phone captures proving that black surfaces, fuzziness and minimize/resume rendering failures are resolved. Existing first-person framing and repetitive wood treatment remain visible quality refinements."
    },
    "thinkingOutOfTheBox": {
      "grade": "B+",
      "evidence": "The implementation combines transaction-complete storage publication, worker identity guards, explicit cancellation, portable export/retry and fresh-engine graphics recovery while preserving nonrectangular selection state and both history stacks. The separate worker in the entry fixture provides a useful deterministic stale-result probe. This is practical integration, with the caveat that manually dispatching the stale event does not establish spontaneous post-termination browser delivery."
    }
  },
  "blockingFindings": [
    "MRR-01 remains open: run the final served build on the affected physical Android/Brave phone and record device/browser, completed-frame timing, drawing-buffer/CSS dimensions and the results for None and available quality modes. Exercise background/minimize, resume, enter/return and continued authoring. Desktop GPU emulation and the older LAN preview do not close this requirement.",
    "MRR-03 is improved but remains open for full-scope acceptance: add a named-room-plan graphics-loss case with a selected nested object and fresh rendered picking, and exercise any required blocked/quota database path separately from deterministic read abort and size-preflight instrumentation. Preserve exact world, history, selection and retry behavior in those cases.",
    "MRR-04 remains open: provide top/orbit/fly/walk and grazing-angle comparisons on the same surfaces, including restored styles, with legible phone-density captures. Address or explicitly accept the ceiling-heavy first-person framing and repetitive wood treatment. The shader correction is source evidence for a numerical risk reduction, not proof that the affected-phone visual symptom is cured."
  ],
  "resolvedFindings": [
    "The saved-workspace correction closes the prior transaction-lifetime defect: a successful get request cannot begin world admission before its transaction completes, and abort/requesterror/synchronous JavaScript failures retain the prior checkpoint and expose retry.",
    "The five retained storage cases pass 35 checks for queued save, immediate read abort, abort after read success, synchronous read failure and size preflight, comparing persisted and live world/history/future/selection/camera data and exercising retry.",
    "The retained delayed-entry journey passes 24 checks through background cancellation and actual WebGL-loss reload, preserving a nonrectangular mask, both history stacks and the exterior world before a successful retry. The stale valid response is intentionally injected into the terminated worker event target and is documented as such.",
    "The release build and application provenance bind the corrected source and generated artifacts; the final entry metrics report no browser errors and zero live framebuffers after recovery. These desktop metrics are not phone performance measurements."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is a retained-evidence re-review; Luna did not rerun the browser, native or GPU suites because the reviewed source and evidence were frozen and the targeted successful runs were available.",
    "The 35 storage checks and 24 entry checks use deterministic instrumentation under desktop Chromium. They do not measure physical-phone GPU precision, thermal behavior, OS process discard, physical FPS or spontaneous browser delivery of a late event after worker termination.",
    "The storage fault cases cover read/write transaction boundaries and size preflight, but do not by themselves establish behavior for every browser quota or blocked-database condition. The entry case does not cover named-room-plan loss with fresh picking.",
    "The complete feature remains broader than this correction: full mobile visual quality, affected-device recovery, audio/performance acceptance and unrelated catalog/world requirements remain separate gates."
  ],
  "verification": "Independent Luna source review of src/phanes.session.ui.pas confirms transaction-complete FPending publication and requesterror/abort/synchronous-throw handling. Retained builder executions pass 35 storage checks in build/recovery-storage-final-01 (build/recovery-storage-final-01/provenance.json) and 24 entry checks in build/logs/recovery-entry-02.log with no recorded browser errors in build/recovery-entry-02/before-loss-errors.json. The release build succeeds in build/logs/recovery-read-main-build-01.log and is bound by build/recovery-read-provenance-01.json. The current registry contains 127 unique existing inputs; this report fingerprints those declared inputs in reviewedFiles and separately retains 24 cited recovery provenance/result artifact hashes in evidenceFingerprints. No browser or GPU suite was rerun by this critic.",
